F-0229 postfix — .proof-os/gates/build.sh
dev, 2026-08-18, task T-BRANDOPEN-0817

WHAT CHANGED
  1. env_issue no longer gets to overrule a runner that reported. New rule:
     if the test output carries the runner's own tally (`Test Files`/`Tests `/
     `Suites:`/`N passed|failed`), the runner RAN, so a non-zero exit is a finding
     about the code and no environment heuristic may reclassify it. env_issue is
     consulted only when there is no summary at all.
  2. The bare token `network` is gone from env_issue even in that branch.
     npm's real registry failures already match registry.npmjs / ETIMEDOUT /
     ENOTFOUND; `network` only ever matched test output.
  3. Per-leg budgets, each named in its message. tsc/build keep PROOF_GATE_TIMEOUT
     (300s, measured headroom ~5x). The test leg gets PROOF_GATE_TEST_TIMEOUT,
     default 600s — ~6x the measured 99s solo, NOT the 900s an earlier edit set on
     evidence that does not reproduce.
  4. The test leg is SERIALISED (gates/_lock.sh, mkdir-atomic, dead holders reaped
     by pid). Two agents queue instead of starving each other. The lock wait has
     its OWN ceiling (PROOF_GATE_LOCK_WAIT, 900s) and is not charged against the
     leg budget. Failing to get the lock is unavailable, never a pass.
  5. Per-leg verdict table on every exit path, so one unavailable leg no longer
     erases the two that proved.
  6. rc/liveness wired (F-0026): $SELF resolved before the cd, rc_init after it,
     _rc.sh located in the project gates dir or the synced plugin, no-op if absent.

